Windows VM Testing To Be Done
=============================

Before switching the Windows VM to Bridged Adapter networking, finish these local-only sanity checks.

1. Launch behavior
   Run from the Start Menu shortcut, Desktop shortcut if created, and installed path. Confirm tray icon appears and browser opens http://127.0.0.1:3000.

2. Quit behavior
   Use tray Quit. Confirm minnty_sound_server.exe disappears from Task Manager.

3. Relaunch behavior
   Launch again after Quit. Confirm no duplicate/conflicting server and UI still loads.

4. Reboot persistence
   Reboot VM. Confirm app does not auto-start unless expected. Launch manually and verify same behavior.

5. Uninstall
   Use Windows Apps/Programs uninstall. Confirm app folder and shortcuts are removed. Reinstall if continuing tests.

6. Portable zip path
   Optionally test portable zip still behaves as documented now that the VC++ Redistributable is installed by the installer.

7. SmartScreen notes
   Record actual Edge/SmartScreen wording for installer zip extraction/run, so README/release notes can be accurate later.

8. Basic UI behavior
   Open UI, switch theme, view devices, change frame duration, start/stop calibration stream, confirm no obvious browser errors.

9. Audio inside VM
   Play audio in Edge/Media Player, confirm meters show activity. VM audio is not perfect, so treat this as smoke test only.

10. Snapshot
    Take a VM snapshot named installed-local-ok before changing networking.
